  "tradeoffs": {
    "C01": "SURVIVE: Fastest candidate (0.084 s/image), with 20.33% mean small-component recall and 4239 completely missed small components. Whole-image IoU is lower than the palette leaders. Retain the weak tile-winner observation family to improve coarse-label learning rather than just boundary geometry.",
    "C02": "REJECT: Cross-fitted trust does not improve aggregate IoU, speed or small-component recall over C01. Held-out support can downweight valid rare appearances without recovering missing anatomy.",
    "C03": "SURVIVE: Local appearance shrinkage reaches 0.66871 mean IoU and 19.81% small-component recall, with relatively strong TIGER performance. Its 0.969 s/image cost is the major limitation. Retain the spatially varying statistical-model family to test faster and less biased local evidence.",
    "C04": "REJECT: Pairwise logistic coupling is worse than C01 in mean IoU, speed and small-component recall. Extra independent class contrasts do not solve information loss or rare-class supervision.",
    "C05": "REJECT: Second-order colour texture is dominated by C01 across primary accuracy, time and small-component recall. The selected texture statistics can blur the few structures missing from converted RGB.",
    "C06": "REJECT: Sparse patch dictionaries lower mean IoU while taking more time than C01; native reviews show no consistent recovery of fine missing tissue regions. Do not add patch-reconstruction complexity without a demonstrated benefit.",
    "C07": "REJECT: Low-rank probability patches slightly improve B22 but are slower, less accurate and marginally worse at small-component recall than C17. Review does not establish a distinct anatomical gain.",
    "C08": "REJECT: Haar coefficient shrinkage is dominated by C17 in mean IoU, runtime and small-component recall. Small detail suppression does not recover anatomy absent from RGB.",
    "C09": "REJECT: Minimum-description quadtree produces visible square architecture and has only 15.55% small-component recall. It is slower and less accurate than C01, with reduced fine-region preservation.",
    "C10": "REJECT: Duration-aware axis inference is close to the accuracy leaders but costs 0.509 s/image. The very small recall difference relative to C17 does not offset 4529 completely missed small components or directional structural risk.",
    "C11": "REJECT: Continuous spline fields sometimes improve broad simple TIGER cases, but erase intricate architecture and enlarge rare foci across BCSS/TIGER. Mean IoU and 13.68% small-component recall are weak; sparse-reference near-perfect scores do not validate unscored anatomy.",
    "C12": "REJECT: Coarse triad motifs do not improve mean IoU over B22 and reduce small-component recall to 17.38%. Reintroducing coarse geometric patterns is unsupported by the visual review.",
    "C13": "REJECT: Expected-count macro-IoU assignment loses primary IoU relative to C17 and C18 and costs more. Its modest small-component benefit is weaker than C01, C03 and C15; miscalibration can enlarge rare classes.",
    "C14": "REJECT: Feasible palette bounds retain 19.55% small-component recall but score slightly below C03 and cost much more than C17. No unique consistent recovery in native review justifies keeping another palette family alongside exact and adaptive solutions.",
    "C15": "SURVIVE: Copula likelihood has the highest mean small-component recall (22.56%) and the fewest completely missed small components (4233). Primary IoU is only 0.64494 and visual review shows false chromatic rims and region expansion. Retain only as the non-Gaussian density family; the next changes must address these explicit false-positive risks.",
    "C16": "REJECT: Delete-tile influence penalties do not improve mean IoU over the palette leaders and have weaker small-component recall than C01. Penalizing rare tile dependence can reject valid small appearances.",
    "C17": "SURVIVE: Converged fixed-lattice palette optimization achieves 0.67160 mean IoU at 0.142 s/image, about 27% faster than C18 with a 0.000185 IoU difference. Retain this finite-lattice exact-QP operating point alongside C18, explicitly acknowledging their shared palette inverse family.",
    "C18": "SURVIVE: Accuracy leader at 0.67179 mean IoU, required by the preregistered selection rule. Certified adaptive colour precision removes several false third-class rims seen in approximate inversion, but has low small-component recall and cannot restore detail erased by the RGB conversion. Cost is 0.196 s/image.",
    "C19": "REJECT: Adaptive spatial linear evaluation is fast but less accurate than C01 and has lower small-component recall. Finer sampling of the same low-detail RGB cannot create missing anatomical evidence.",
    "C20": "REJECT: Exterior-white removal reduces aggregate IoU and deletes expert-labelled adipose in TIGER28 (approximately 0.83 to 0.60). It simultaneously misses many enclosed white clefts. Brightness plus border connectivity cannot determine whether a white area is glass, fat or lumen."
  },
